# netsurf: form controls' values as browsers have them -- textarea,
# select, option; HTML's selectedness for a select (patch 287)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 286)
#
# `value` was one accessor on every element, its value attribute (the
# bridge's generic reflection). So a textarea read "" -- its value is its
# text, then what is typed or set -- and a value a script gave it was not
# what the field showed or the form sent (doc 10, 283's "found, not
# fixed"); a <select> had no options, selectedIndex, value, length or
# type; option.selected / value / index were missing or read attributes;
# a checkbox without a value attribute read "" (browsers: "on"); a <div>
# had a value. Checked against Chromium case by case:
#
#  - vita_polyfill.js, "form controls' values": textarea value (newlines
#    as LF), defaultValue (its text), textLength; select options (an
#    HTMLOptionsCollection, live, by index too, item / namedItem / add /
#    remove / length), selectedIndex, value, selectedOptions, length, type,
#    multiple, size, form, item, namedItem, add, remove(i); option value
#    (else its text, whitespace collapsed), text, label, selected,
#    defaultSelected, disabled, index, form; checkbox / radio "on"; button,
#    data, param, li (a number), output, meter (a number within min..max)
#    each their own value; no other element has one.
#  - macsurf_qjs.c __vitaFormCtl: a textarea's value read and set through
#    libdom (286) and a select's selection read and picked; the control's
#    gadget, when laid out, shows the change (form_gadget_sync_with_dom,
#    form_select_apply_dom).
#  - form.c form_select_selectedness: which options are selected, as HTML
#    decides it -- in a drop-down the last option marked selected, else
#    its first enabled one (unless a script left it with none) -- used by
#    the gadget, the submission and scripts alike. The submission sent
#    every option marked selected (a drop-down with two sent both) and
#    nothing when the first option was disabled and none marked; the gadget
#    took the first marked, or the first option disabled or not (and marked
#    it in the DOM). A pick from the menu unmarks every other option in a
#    drop-down, not only the one shown.
#
# An input's value stays its value attribute, the engine's model (a value
# a script sets is shown and sent, but is also the attribute and
# defaultValue -- unlike browsers). A select cannot be picked from on the
# Vita: the frontend has no select menu (older than this; script-driven
# selects now work).
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-form-values.html (FORMVAL 8/8, Chromium 8/8)
# and tools/run-vita-sim.sh "scriptless form
# submissions" case "values" (a script's textarea / select / option values
# submitted, digest equal to Chromium's).
